robes (bridge-probe, reconcile dry-run), not pytest.`"],"finding":"The bridge-probe -> bridge check-access inventory omits two CI workflow comment sites and one in-tree docstring that reference `bridge-probe`. `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:692` ('manual probe (bridge-probe / reconcile dry-run)') and `.github/workflows/test.yml:10` ('manual probes (bridge-probe, reconcile dry-run)') both name the verb; `docs/user-guide.md:393` names `rebar bridge-probe`. None appear in the enumerated CLI/Docs/Tests lists, which only cite the reconcile-bridge-canary workflow.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fffaef271da154aa6","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Enumerated consumers — `bridge-probe` -> `bridge check-access`","norm_id":"n538ff33e6506a822","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml:692 keeps a stale `bridge-probe` reference after rename",".github/workflows/test.yml:10 keeps a stale `bridge-probe` reference after rename","docs/user-guide.md:393 keeps a stale primary spelling that the stale-usage grep AC may flag"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the intended default for `bridge setup`'s help integration (e.g. preserve the existing intercept shape with argparse-owned --help and no pinned .txt) rather than leaving the intercept-vs-full-registration choice to the executor.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7","T9"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"Moving it under the bridge noun must either preserve that intercept shape or wire overview + routing + a .txt together — adding a .txt alone BREAKS test_help_overview_coverage.\"","This is a real design choice (intercept vs. full-verb registration) left to the executor rather than decided in the plan."],"finding":"The plan defers the architecture choice for how `jira-onboard`/`bridge setup` fits the help system to the executor: it must 'either preserve that intercept shape or wire overview + routing + a .txt together' without stating which is the intended default.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb20d91eeec736746","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Enumerated consumers — jira-onboard -> bridge setup (NOTE paragraph)","norm_id":"nd4e1011b291a2f3a","priority":0.201,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["Executor picks the full-registration path, must invent overview+routing+.txt wiring not otherwise specified, diverging from the b5db-7433 intercept precedent."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Pick the intercept-preserving path as the default given the b5db-7433 precedent, and note the alternative only as an explicit fallback if a .txt is required.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Commit `bridge setup` to ONE dispatch shape: state whether it remains a top-level-style intercept re-exposed under the `bridge` prefix (preserving argparse-owned --help and no overview/.txt entry) or becomes a genuine `bridge` subparser command, and spell out the resulting overview/routing/.txt obligations so test_help_overview_coverage stays green.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Moving it under the `bridge` noun must either preserve that intercept shape or wire overview + routing + a `.txt` together — adding a `.txt` alone BREAKS test_help_overview_coverage.'","Live code: `jira-onboard` is a top-level intercept (src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py:586) that calls jira_onboard(argv[1:]) directly, bypassing bridge_cli's argparse subparser group (_bridge_commands.py:194-215) that `bridge fsck` uses via _dispatch_bridge (:250).","The two mechanisms differ structurally (intercept vs. subparser), so 'bridge setup' cannot simply be added to _BRIDGE_MODES without deciding which shape it takes."],"finding":"The plan raises but does not resolve the structural mechanism question of how `bridge setup` reconciles the existing intercept shape (argparse owns --help, intentionally no overview/help .txt per b5db-7433) with the argparse-subparser-based `bridge` noun group that `bridge fsck`/`bridge check-access` route through; it offers an unresolved either/or.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc5b0096f80754fb2","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Section 'Enumerated consumers — jira-onboard -> bridge setup' and AC line 1","norm_id":"nd48f18b221da0525","priority":0.2382,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["Implementer wires `bridge setup` as a bridge subparser command, losing the wizard's argparse --help ownership or double-parsing argv","Implementer adds help/bridge-setup.txt to satisfy consistency and breaks test_help_overview_coverage"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4444,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v4","material_fingerprint":"6f2ab46a9863805e","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["819491e0132dc913",10442],"file_impact":["a1d1d8b40cdb4dd9",36],"ticket_id":["f60cae4609dbc3ed",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":794238,"cache_write_tokens":261987,"claim_path":"no-